B.X1=s(["The system is working normally \u2014 document the finding","There is an air leak \u2014 tape all the connections","The tubing is blocked \u2014 vigorously milk the tubing","The suction pressure is set too high"],t.s)
B.cl=new A.J(1,0.7058823529411765,0.27058823529411763,0.22745098039215686,B.h)
B.dd=new A.Mj(0,"connected")
B.aq5=new A.hd("The water in the water-seal chamber rises and falls gently each time the patient breathes.","What does this finding indicate?",B.X1,"Gentle rise and fall with breathing (tidaling) shows the system is patent and pressure changes are reaching the pleural space \u2014 this is normal and simply documented. Milking or stripping tubing creates dangerous negative pressure and needs an order.",!0,!1,!0,0.25,B.cl,B.dd)
B.a0h=s(["Check the tubing and connections for an air leak","Clamp the chest tube immediately","Turn up the wall suction","Document this as normal water-seal activity"],t.s)
B.aq2=new A.hd("You notice continuous, vigorous bubbling in the water-seal chamber even between breaths.","What should the nurse do FIRST?",B.a0h,"Continuous bubbling in the water seal means air is leaking into the system, so the nurse starts at the dressing and works toward the unit checking every connection. Clamping traps air and risks a tension pneumothorax; continuous bubbling is only normal in the suction-control chamber.",!1,!0,!0,0.25,B.cl,B.dd)
B.VO=s(["The lung has re-expanded \u2014 assess and notify the provider","There is a large air leak in the system","The suction is set too low","The patient is developing a tension pneumothorax"],t.s)
B.aqa=new A.hd("Three days after insertion, tidaling has stopped. The patient is breathing comfortably with clear, equal breath sounds.","What is the most likely explanation?",B.VO,"When the lung fully re-expands there is no more air or pressure change to transmit, so tidaling stops \u2014 in a comfortable patient with clear breath sounds this signals readiness for tube removal. A kinked or occluded tube also stops tidaling, so the nurse still checks the tubing, but distress would accompany tension pneumothorax.",!1,!1,!0,0.25,B.cl,B.dd)
B.Z3=s(["Notify the surgeon immediately","Document the expected postoperative drainage","Empty the collection chamber and continue monitoring","Clamp the tube to slow the bleeding"],t.s)
B.aq9=new A.hd("One hour after chest surgery, the collection chamber has filled with 220 mL of bright red drainage.","What is the priority action?",B.Z3,"Drainage over about 100 mL per hour, or drainage that is bright red, suggests active hemorrhage and must be reported immediately. Chest drainage units are never emptied at the bedside, and clamping does not stop pleural bleeding \u2014 it hides it.",!1,!1,!0,0.8,B.m3,B.dd)
B.Yk=s(["Submerge the tube end in a bottle of sterile water","Clamp the chest tube until a new unit arrives","Reconnect the tube to the contaminated tubing","Cover the chest insertion site with petroleum gauze"],t.s)
B.GN=new A.Mj(1,"offUnit")
B.aqc=new A.hd("The chest tube disconnects from the drainage unit and the end falls onto the floor.","What should the nurse do FIRST?",B.Yk,"Placing the open tube end 1-2 inches into sterile water instantly restores a water seal so air cannot enter the chest. Clamping risks tension pneumothorax, the contaminated tubing cannot be reused, and petroleum gauze is the response when the tube pulls out of the CHEST, not out of the unit.",!1,!1,!1,0.25,B.cl,B.GN)
B.YU=s(["Cover the site with petroleum gauze taped on three sides","Submerge the tube in sterile water","Pack the wound with dry sterile gauze sealed on all four sides","Leave the site open and raise the head of the bed"],t.s)
B.GO=new A.Mj(2,"outOfChest")
B.aq6=new A.hd("While the patient is turning in bed, the chest tube is accidentally pulled out of the chest wall.","What should the nurse do FIRST?",B.YU,"An occlusive petroleum dressing taped on three sides lets air escape on exhalation but stops it entering on inhalation, preventing tension pneumothorax while the provider is called. Sealing all four sides can trap air; the tube itself is now out, so the water seal no longer helps.",!1,!1,!1,0.3,B.cl,B.GO)
B.a0_=s(["Normal \u2014 this shows suction is being applied correctly","An air leak that must be located immediately","The chamber needs more water added right away","The chest tube has migrated out of position"],t.s)
B.aq_=new A.hd("There is gentle, continuous bubbling in the suction-control chamber while wall suction is running.","How should the nurse interpret this?",B.a0_,"Gentle continuous bubbling is expected in the suction-control chamber when connected to suction \u2014 vigorous bubbling only wastes water through evaporation. Continuous bubbling is a problem in the WATER-SEAL chamber, where it means an air leak.",!0,!1,!0,0.25,B.cl,B.dd)
B.a_d=s(["Clamping the chest tube with hemostats until the new unit arrives","Placing the end of the chest tube about 1 inch under sterile water","Keeping the sterile water bottle below the level of the chest","Assessing respiratory effort and oxygen saturation"],t.s)
B.aq1=new A.hd("The client is walking in the hall with the unit on water seal (no suction) when the chest tube separates from the drainage tubing. A new sterile unit is on its way.","Which action by the nurse requires intervention?",B.a_d,"Clamping for the minutes it takes a new unit to arrive leaves air no way out of the pleural space and can cause a tension pneumothorax, so it must be stopped. Submerging the tube end about 1 inch in sterile water creates an instant water seal, and keeping the bottle below chest level stops water being drawn toward the chest. Assessing breathing is exactly right.",!1,!1,!1,0.25,B.cl,B.GN)
B.Y4=s(["Notify the provider and watch closely for signs of tension pneumothorax","Tape down the fourth side so the dressing is completely airtight","Clean the tube and reinsert it through the same opening","Document the event and reassess at the next scheduled check"],t.s)
B.aq0=new A.hd("A confused client on water seal pulled the chest tube out of the chest wall. You have already covered the site with a sterile occlusive dressing taped on three sides.","What should the nurse do NEXT?",B.Y4,"The provider must be notified right away to decide on a new tube, while the nurse watches for worsening dyspnea, tracheal deviation or falling oxygen saturation. The untaped side acts as a flutter valve that lets air escape, so taping all four sides can trap air \u2014 and if tension signs appear, lift the dressing to release it. A dislodged tube is never reinserted.",!1,!1,!1,0.3,B.cl,B.GO)
B.Zf=s(["Check the tubing for kinks, clots, a dependent loop, or the client lying on it","Document that the lung has re-expanded","Clamp the tube and prepare for its removal","Increase the suction to restart the tidaling"],t.s)
B.aq3=new A.hd("Six hours after a chest tube was placed for a pneumothorax, the water-seal level suddenly stops rising and falling. Breath sounds are still diminished on the affected side.","What should the nurse do FIRST?",B.Zf,"Tidaling that stops suddenly within hours, while breath sounds are still diminished, points to an obstruction: a kink, a clot, the client lying on the tube, or fluid pooled in a dependent loop. Re-expansion stops tidaling gradually over days as breath sounds return, and is only assumed once the tubing is confirmed patent. Clamping or raising suction does nothing to clear a blocked tube.",!1,!1,!0,0.1,B.cl,B.dd)
B.a0y=s(["Notify the surgeon now with the hourly drainage and vital signs","Mark the level and recheck in 1 hour to confirm the trend","Strip the tubing vigorously to keep up with the blood flow","Document it as expected drainage for the first postoperative hours"],t.s)
B.aq4=new A.hd("Two hours after coronary artery bypass surgery, the mediastinal tube drained 70 mL the first hour and 160 mL of bright red blood this hour. Heart rate has risen from 88 to 114.","What is the priority action?",B.a0y,"Output over 100 mL per hour of bright red blood after cardiac surgery, with a rising heart rate, signals active bleeding that may need a return to surgery, so the surgeon is called immediately. Waiting an hour to confirm the trend risks hundreds more milliliters of blood loss or cardiac tamponade. Stripping creates dangerously high negative pressure and is done only per order.",!1,!1,!0,0.8,B.m3,B.dd)
B.VI=s(["Check both water chambers for lost fluid, assess the client, and notify the provider if the water seal was lost","Clamp the chest tube until a new drainage unit is set up","Tilt the unit so spilled drainage runs back into the first column","Document the event \u2014 the unit works normally once it is upright"],t.s)
B.aq7=new A.hd("A visitor bumped the chest drainage unit and it tipped onto its side. You set it back upright right away.","What should the nurse do NEXT?",B.VI,"Tipping can spill water out of the water-seal and suction-control chambers, so after setting the unit upright the nurse checks each fill line, assesses breathing, and notifies the provider (replacing the unit per policy) if the seal was lost. Being upright does not prove the seal is intact, so documenting alone is not enough. Clamping risks tension pneumothorax, and tilting spills more water.",!0,!1,!0,0.25,B.cl,B.dd)
B.a0H=s(["Keep the unit upright and below chest level, with the tube unclamped","Clamp the chest tube for the trip to prevent backflow","Place the unit on the stretcher at the client's feet so it cannot fall","Lay the unit on its side under the stretcher so it cannot tip"],t.s)
B.aqb=new A.hd("The client is going to radiology by stretcher. Per the order, the unit has been disconnected from wall suction, with the suction port left open, and is working on water seal.","Which action is correct during transport?",B.a0H,"The unit must stay upright and below the chest so air and fluid drain away from the pleural space and nothing siphons back. Clamping during transport blocks air from escaping and can cause a tension pneumothorax. A unit resting on a flat stretcher sits level with the chest, and a unit on its side loses its water seal.",!0,!1,!1,0.25,B.cl,B.dd)
B.Ys=s(["Check that wall suction is on, connected, and high enough to produce gentle bubbling","Add sterile water above the 20 cm line to increase the suction","Document it as normal \u2014 no bubbling means there is no air leak","Clamp the chest tube and notify the provider"],t.s)
B.aq8=new A.hd("Suction of 20 cm H2O is ordered. The suction-control chamber of the wet suction system is filled to the 20 cm line, but there is no bubbling in it at all.","What should the nurse do FIRST?",B.Ys,'In a wet suction system the water height sets the suction, and gentle, continuous bubbling shows the wall suction is actually reaching the chamber. No bubbling means the wall source is off, too low or disconnected, so the nurse checks and adjusts it. Adding water changes the ordered pressure, and "no bubbling is good" applies to the water-seal chamber, not the suction chamber.',!0,!1,!1,0.25,B.cl,B.dd)
B.uF=s([B.aq5,B.aq2,B.aqa,B.aq9,B.aqc,B.aq6,B.aq_,B.aq1,B.aq0,B.aq3,B.aq4,B.aq7,B.aqb,B.aq8],A.aj("w<hd>"))
B.Wx=s(["Perform hand hygiene","Put on the gown and tie it at the neck and waist","Apply the mask or N95 respirator and check the seal","Put on goggles or a face shield","Put on gloves, pulling them over the gown cuffs"],t.s)
B.asg=new A.fX("ppe_don","Donning PPE","Don: Gown \u2192 Mask \u2192 Goggles \u2192 Gloves. Gloves always go on last so they cover the gown cuffs.",B.Wx)
B.Yd=s(["Remove gloves, peeling glove-to-glove then skin-to-skin","Remove goggles by the headband without touching the front","Untie and remove the gown, rolling it inside out","Remove the mask by the ties without touching the front","Perform hand hygiene"],t.s)
B.aso=new A.fX("ppe_doff","Doffing PPE","Doff: Gloves \u2192 Goggles \u2192 Gown \u2192 Mask, then hand hygiene. The mask comes off LAST, touching only the ties.",B.Yd)
B.a14=s(["Position the patient in high Fowler's and agree on a stop signal","Measure the tube from nose tip to earlobe to xiphoid process","Lubricate the tip with water-soluble lubricant","Insert along the floor of the nostril; when the tube reaches the throat, have the patient flex the head and sip water","Advance to the marked length and check for distress","Verify placement (aspirate pH / X-ray per policy), then secure the tube to the nose"],t.s)
B.asp=new A.fX("ng_insert","Inserting an NG Tube","Measure nose \u2192 earlobe \u2192 xiphoid. Have the patient sip water and flex the head forward as the tube passes the nasopharynx.",B.a14)
B.Z7=s(["Verify consent, order, and baseline vital signs","With a second nurse, match the unit to the patient ID band and crossmatch record at the bedside","Prime Y-tubing with 0.9% normal saline only","Begin the transfusion slowly (about 2 mL/min)","Stay with the patient and recheck vitals after 15 minutes","If a reaction occurs: STOP the blood, keep the line open with saline, and notify the provider and blood bank"],t.s)
B.asr=new A.fX("transfusion","Starting a Blood Transfusion","Two RNs verify at the bedside. Stay with the patient for the first 15 minutes \u2014 that is when reactions strike.",B.Z7)
B.VL=s(["Perform hand hygiene and prepare the medication with a fresh needle","Select and clean the ventrogluteal site","Pull the skin about 1 inch to the side and hold it","Insert the needle at 90 degrees and inject slowly","Wait 10 seconds, withdraw the needle, then release the skin","Do not massage the site; document the injection"],t.s)
B.ash=new A.fX("ztrack","Z-Track IM Injection","Z-track seals irritating medication in the muscle. Never massage the site afterward.",B.VL)
B.Wg=s(["Perform hand hygiene and open the outer package on a clean, dry surface","Open the inner wrapper like a book without reaching over the field","Pick up the first glove by the folded cuff (inside surface) only","Slide the dominant hand in without touching the outside","Slip the gloved fingers under the second glove's cuff (outside surface) and pull it on","Adjust both gloves touching only sterile glove to sterile glove"],t.s)
B.ass=new A.fX("sterile_gloves","Applying Sterile Gloves","Glove-to-glove, skin-to-skin: bare hands touch only the inside cuff; the gloved hand touches only sterile surfaces.",B.Wg)
B.a0G=s(["Verify the order, identify the client, explain the procedure, and perform hand hygiene","Position the client supine with knees bent and apart, and wash the perineum with soap and water","Perform hand hygiene, open the kit with sterile technique, put on sterile gloves, place the drape, and lubricate the catheter tip","Separate the labia with the non-dominant hand and clean front to back, using a new swab for each stroke","Insert the catheter 2 to 3 inches until urine flows, then advance it 1 to 2 inches farther","Inflate the balloon with the prefilled sterile water, then gently pull back until you feel resistance","Secure the catheter to the inner thigh and hang the bag below bladder level, off the floor"],t.s)
B.asf=new A.fX("foley_female","Inserting a Urinary Catheter (Female)","Once your non-dominant hand separates the labia it stays there and is no longer sterile, so prepare the kit first. If the catheter enters the vagina, leave it as a landmark and insert a new sterile catheter.",B.a0G)
B.a_k=s(["Perform hand hygiene, explain the procedure, place the client in semi-Fowler's, and set wall suction below 150 mm Hg","Open the sterile kit, put on sterile gloves, connect the catheter, and preoxygenate with 100% oxygen for 30 to 60 seconds","Gently insert the catheter into the tracheostomy with NO suction applied","Apply intermittent suction while rotating and withdrawing the catheter, for no longer than 10 seconds","Reoxygenate and let oxygen saturation return to baseline before another pass, limiting to 2 or 3 passes","Suction the mouth last if needed, discard the catheter, reassess breath sounds, and document"],t.s)
B.asq=new A.fX("trach_suction","Tracheostomy Suctioning","Suction on the way OUT, never on the way in, for no more than 10 seconds a pass. Oxygenate before and between passes, and suction the trach before the mouth \u2014 never the reverse with the same catheter.",B.a_k)
B.a0l=s(["Perform hand hygiene, explain the procedure, and put a mask on yourself and the client (or have the client turn away)","Put on clean gloves, peel the old dressing toward the insertion site, and inspect the site","Remove the gloves, perform hand hygiene, open the sterile kit, and put on sterile gloves","Scrub the site with chlorhexidine using back-and-forth friction for 30 seconds","Let the chlorhexidine air-dry completely \u2014 do not blot or fan it","Apply a sterile transparent dressing centered over the insertion site","Label the dressing with the date, time and your initials, then document the site assessment"],t.s)
B.ask=new A.fX("cvc_dressing","Central Line Dressing Change","Mask on, peel toward the insertion site, scrub chlorhexidine for 30 seconds and let it DRY. Change a transparent dressing every 7 days, or sooner if it is damp, loose or soiled.",B.a0l)
B.ZK=s(["Check the order and timing (before meals, coordinated with the tray), identify the client, and perform hand hygiene","Put on clean gloves and clean the side of a fingertip, letting it dry completely","Insert an in-date test strip into the meter, then puncture the side of the fingertip with a single-use lancet","Wipe away the first drop if the device instructions say to, then let a hanging drop form without squeezing hard","Touch the test strip to the drop and let it draw in enough blood","Apply pressure with gauze, discard the lancet in a sharps container, then record and act on the result per protocol"],t.s)
B.asj=new A.fX("glucose_check","Fingerstick Blood Glucose","Use the side of the fingertip, not the pad \u2014 it has fewer nerve endings. Squeezing hard pushes tissue fluid into the drop and can give a falsely low reading; wet alcohol can skew it too.",B.ZK)
B.Zo=s(["Check the order, the client's current blood glucose, and that a meal is coming if it is mealtime insulin","Draw up the dose and have a second nurse independently verify it if policy requires","Identify the client with two identifiers, put on gloves, and choose a site rotated from the last injection","Clean the site with alcohol and let it dry","Pinch up the skin and insert the needle at 90 degrees, or 45 degrees for a thin client with little subcutaneous tissue","Inject the insulin steadily without aspirating","Withdraw the needle, do not massage the site, and activate the needle safety device","Document the dose and site, and monitor for hypoglycemia when the insulin peaks"],t.s)
B.asn=new A.fX("subq_insulin","Subcutaneous Insulin Injection","Insulin is a high-alert drug: get an independent double-check where policy requires. Rotate sites within one body area to prevent lipohypertrophy, and never aspirate or massage.",B.Zo)
B.Xu=s(["Check the order for the drug and which eye, identify the client, perform hand hygiene, and put on gloves","Clean any drainage from the eyelid, wiping from the inner to the outer corner","Have the client tilt the head back and look up, and gently pull the lower lid down to form a pocket","Holding the dropper above the eye without touching it, instill the drop into the conjunctival sac \u2014 not onto the cornea","Have the client close the eye gently without squeezing, and press on the inner corner for 30 to 60 seconds","Wait at least 5 minutes before instilling a different eye drop, and document each medication"],t.s)
B.asl=new A.fX("eye_drops","Administering Eye Drops","Drop into the lower-lid pocket, never onto the cornea. Press the inner corner of the eye to keep the drug out of the tear duct and bloodstream, and wait 5 minutes between different drops.",B.Xu)
B.Xt=s(["Make sure the scene is safe, then tap and shout; if there is no response, call for help and send someone for the AED","Check for no breathing or only gasping and for a carotid pulse at the same time, taking no more than 10 seconds","Start compressions on the lower half of the sternum: 100 to 120 per minute, at least 2 inches deep, with full recoil","After every 30 compressions, open the airway with a head tilt-chin lift and give 2 breaths, each over 1 second","As soon as the AED arrives, turn it on and attach the pads to the bare, dry chest","Make sure no one touches the client while the AED analyzes, then deliver a shock if advised","Resume CPR immediately, starting with compressions, and follow the AED prompts every 2 minutes"],t.s)
B.asi=new A.fX("cpr_aed","Adult CPR with an AED","Push hard, at least 2 inches, and fast, 100 to 120 per minute, letting the chest fully recoil. Use the AED the moment it arrives and restart compressions right after the shock.",B.Xt)
B.Vi=s(["Assess the cause of the behavior and try less restrictive alternatives first, such as reorientation or a sitter","Obtain a provider order that states the reason and a time limit","Explain the reason to the client, then apply the padded restraint so two fingers slide underneath","Tie the strap to the movable part of the bed frame, not the side rail, with a quick-release knot","Place the call light within reach and check circulation, sensation and skin on the facility schedule","Release the restraint on schedule, one limb at a time, for range of motion, toileting, fluids and skin care","Document alternatives tried, each check and the client's response, and remove the restraint as soon as possible"],t.s)
B.asm=new A.fX("restraints","Applying Soft Wrist Restraints","Restraints are a last resort and need an order with a time limit \u2014 never PRN. Tie a quick-release knot to the bed FRAME, never the side rail, and keep two fingers of room under the cuff.",B.Vi)
